; minibuffer fills ask's line reader: a default answers an empty input,
; and M-n inserts it past what was typed.
> (define t (start! (lambda () (ask:line "Rename to (default notes): " "notes"))))
> (press! "RET")
> (result t)
"notes"
> (define t (start! (lambda () (ask:line "Rename to (default notes): " "notes"))))
> (press! "M-n")
> (input)
"notes"
> (type! "-old")
> (press! "RET")
> (result t)
"notes-old"
; Without a default, an empty input answers itself.
> (define t (start! (lambda () (ask:line "Rename to: "))))
> (press! "RET")
> (result t)
""
